From: Maximilian Gaedig <sly-keg-cheating@duck.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm845: active-only XO for UFS and USB HS PHYs

clk-rpmh gives the plain rpmhcc XO valid_state_mask = WAKE|ACTIVE|SLEEP,
while the _A variant votes WAKE|ACTIVE only, so any AP-side reference on the
plain clock writes xo.lvl = 0x3 ("on") into the RPMH sleep set. AOSS only
reaches its deep states with XO released, so this pins qcom_stats aosd and
cxsd at 0 together.

The UFS host controller, the UFS PHY and both USB HS PHYs take the plain
clock and hold it for their whole lifetime -- the references survive runtime
suspend, and for the USB PHY even survive unbinding the gadget and physically
removing the cable (measured). None of them need the crystal running while
the AP itself is asleep: UFS is in hibern8 (spm_lvl 3) and the USB PHY is
powered down, and XO is restored before the AP touches either on resume.

Measured on a OnePlus 6: bi_tcxo's reference count drops from 302 to 7, and
88e2000.phy / 1d84000.ufshc / phy@1d87000 all move to bi_tcxo_ao. Booting
from UFS with the active-only vote works normally.

Note this is not by itself sufficient: xo.lvl is still 0x3, held by the
remaining functional clocks (display, USB, UFS core, camcc) whose parent is
bi_tcxo. cx.lvl and mx.lvl already vote 0, and every BCM sleep vote is
zero-bandwidth, so XO is the last blocker.

Signed-off-by: Maximilian Gaedig <sly-keg-cheating@duck.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845.dtsi	2026-09-03 00:48:38.895380787 +0200
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845.dtsi	2026-09-03 00:48:38.917811537 +0200
@@ -2683,7 +2683,7 @@
 				<&gcc GCC_AGGRE_UFS_PHY_AXI_CLK>,
 				<&gcc GCC_UFS_PHY_AHB_CLK>,
 				<&gcc GCC_UFS_PHY_UNIPRO_CORE_CLK>,
-				<&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK>,
+				<&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK_A>,
 				<&gcc GCC_UFS_PHY_TX_SYMBOL_0_CLK>,
 				<&gcc GCC_UFS_PHY_RX_SYMBOL_0_CLK>,
 				<&gcc GCC_UFS_PHY_RX_SYMBOL_1_CLK>,
@@ -2732,7 +2732,7 @@
 			compatible = "qcom,sdm845-qmp-ufs-phy";
 			reg = <0 0x01d87000 0 0x1000>;
 
-			clocks = <&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK>,
+			clocks = <&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK_A>,
 				 <&gcc GCC_UFS_PHY_PHY_AUX_CLK>,
 				 <&gcc GCC_UFS_MEM_CLKREF_CLK>;
 			clock-names = "ref",
@@ -4122,7 +4122,7 @@
 			#phy-cells = <0>;
 
 			clocks = <&gcc GCC_USB_PHY_CFG_AHB2PHY_CLK>,
-				 <&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK>;
+				 <&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK_A>;
 			clock-names = "cfg_ahb", "ref";
 
 			resets = <&gcc GCC_QUSB2PHY_PRIM_BCR>;
@@ -4137,7 +4137,7 @@
 			#phy-cells = <0>;
 
 			clocks = <&gcc GCC_USB_PHY_CFG_AHB2PHY_CLK>,
-				 <&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK>;
+				 <&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK_A>;
 			clock-names = "cfg_ahb", "ref";
 
 			resets = <&gcc GCC_QUSB2PHY_SEC_BCR>;
